    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nWelcome to Holywell Avenue, Sea Road, Kilcoole A home that combines coastal living with everyday convenience.\n\n1 Holywell Avenue is a light filled, spacious two-bedroom ground floor, own hall door apartment. Situated in the peaceful Holywell development on Sea Road in Kilcoole with the beach and train within minutes walk and the quaint village of Kilcoole at the top of the road.\nInside, the accommodation is bright, spacious and well laid out. The welcoming living area provides the perfect place to relax or entertain and is full of natural light while the well-appointed kitchen offers practical everyday functionality. Two generous double bedrooms, with the main being en suite, provide peaceful retreats, complemented by a stylish bathroom and excellent storage throughout.\n\nWhether you're taking your first step onto the property ladder, downsizing to a more manageable home or seeking a smart investment opportunity, this apartment delivers easy, low-maintenance living in a highly desirable location.\n\nBeing on the ground floor offers an added level of accessibility and ease, making this an attractive option for buyers at every stage of life.\n\nHolywell Avenue enjoys a superb setting on Sea Road, one of Kilcoole's most sought-after residential locations. From morning walks along the nearby beach to coffee in the village, everything you need is close at hand. Kilcoole offers a wonderful sense of community together with excellent amenities including shops, cafés, schools, sports clubs and public transport, while Greystones, Bray and Dublin are all easily accessible via the nearby N11/M11 and DART services."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHallway - \nLaminate flooring, radiator cover, ceiling coving, central light.\n\nLiving/Dining - \nLaminate flooring, ceiling coving, dual aspect to front and side, cream stone fireplace with black hearth and gas fire inset.\n\nKitchen/Dining - \nLinoleum flooring, cream painted kitchen units, central light, window overlooking rear, stainless steel sink unit and drainer, space for fridge freezer, plumbed for washing machine, Zanussi gas hob and extractor, integrated dishwasher.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nDouble room with laminate flooring, fitted wardrobes, window overlooking rear, wall paneling, central light.\n\nEn suite - \nLaminate flooring, central light, wc, whb with understorage, tiled splashback, Shires shower with rainfall shower head, fully tiled around shower.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nDouble room with laminate flooring, window overlooking front, central light, fitted wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - \nLaminate flooring, radiator cabinet, wc, whb, tiled splashback, bath, window to rear, fully tiled around bath.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Spacious two-bedroom ground floor apartment</li><li> Bright, well-proportioned accommodation</li><li> Open plan living and dining space</li><li> Two generous double bedrooms</li><li> Excellent storage throughout</li><li> Designated parking</li><li> Well-maintained development</li><li> Walking distance to Kilcoole village</li><li> Walking distance to commuter train</li><li> Short drive to Greystones Park & Ride</li><li> Walking distance to the beach and coastal walks</li><li> Excellent transport links to Dublin and Wicklow</li><li> Ideal for first-time buyers, downsizers or investors</ul>"
      },
